        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Some fix candidates. I can try implement the best candidate.\n\n1. `vim.lsp.enable()` (`runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua`): instead of\n   `doautoall('nvim.lsp.enable FileType')`, iterate loaded buffers and re-fire the event\n   only for buffers with `filetype ~= ''`. Re-firing on a buffer whose filetype has not\n   been detected can never match a config anyway.\n2. Core (`src/nvim/autocmd.c:1669`): only set `b_did_filetype` when the FileType event\n   executes for a buffer whose `'filetype'` is non-empty.\n3. `ex_doautoall()` (`src/nvim/autocmd.c`): do not run the event for the current buffer\n   when it is not loaded (consistent with the `b_ml.ml_mfp == NULL` skip for other\n   buffers).",
